   140	The monomial valuation is `val(x^i y^j)=-i+delta_1 j`, so
   141	`h` allows `i <= delta_1(j+1)` and `beta` allows
   142	`i <= delta_1(j+d')`.  The two-point leading form for `delta_2=-1` is
   143	`y^{V_2}(y-x)` when `u'=1`; see lines 213--220 of the same frozen report.
