   157	## Reconstructed Systems
   158	
   159	Branch A computable predecessor.  I used the source-checked two-point
   160	`d'=2,e'=3` A/B system on Moh's transformed row `(27,18;M_2=21,V_2=8;k=4)`.
   161	This is not the omitted ten-coefficient eta-reduced display; it is the
   162	13-coefficient plus Jacobian-constant predecessor under the p.208/p.210
   163	A/B reading.  TYPE: Moh does not print enough to verify that his omitted
   164	ten-coefficient eta system is exactly a specialization of this predecessor,
   165	so the computed kill is reported for the predecessor, not promoted to the
   166	missing display.
   167	
   168	Ring map:
   169	
   170	```text
   171	R = Q[h_0_8,h_0_7,h_0_6,h_0_5,h_0_4,h_0_3,h_0_2,h_0_1,h_0_0,
   172	      bp,bq,br,bs,c,T]
   173	variables x,y are polynomial variables eliminated by coefficient extraction.
   174	
   175	h = y^8(y-x) + h_0_8 y^8 + h_0_7 y^7 + ... + h_0_1 y + h_0_0
   176	A = (h - h|_{y=0})/y
   177	beta = bp A + bq y + br x + bs
   178	f = h^2 + 2 beta
   179	alpha = quotient_y(beta^2, h)
   180	g = h^3 + 3 beta h + (3/2) alpha
   181	E_A = coefficients of J_{x,y}(f,g) - c x^4
   182	saturate by T c - 1.
   183	```
   184	
   185	The extracted `E_A` has 29 generators.  The first generator is `-c`, and
   186	therefore the saturated ideal has the explicit certificate
   187	`1 = -(T c - 1) - T*(-c)`.  Singular's reduced basis is `[1]`.
   188	The unsaturated ideal without `T c - 1` is nontrivial, so the wrapper control
   189	is not vacuous.
