   259	## 5. Typed `u_s>1` procedure
   260	
   261	Input is a screened skeleton `S=(n,m,M_i,d_i,V_i)`, optional actual-disc data
   262	`R` (minor radius/general-point jet and all leading polynomials), and an
   263	optional non-boundary probe `P` such as Moh's p.209 `g`-probe.
   264	
   265	```text
   266	MINOR(S,R,P):
   267	  1. Check every source hypothesis: monic/total-degree condition, delta_s=-1,
   268	     M_s=n-2, the actual minor cluster, and u_s=d_s-v_s>0.
   269	  2. Compute v_s=V_s, u_s=d_s-v_s, q=v_s/u_s.  Compute Def.5.1 delta_i,
   270	     but label them MAJOR; never substitute delta_{s-1} for delta*_{s-1}.
   271	  3. If u_s=1, Prop.6.4 certifies delta*>=q.  Output
   272	     DESCEND-WITH-MODIFIED-HYPOTHESIS via Prop.6.3.
   273	  4. If u_s>1 and R has no actual delta*, use only Prop.6.1's delta*>=1.
   274	     If 1>=q, descend; otherwise output OPEN[MINOR-RADIUS].
   275	  5. If R proves delta*>=q, output DESCEND-WITH-MODIFIED-HYPOTHESIS with
   276	     Prop.6.3's pi-degree tower and monomial Jacobian.
   277	  6. If R proves delta*<q, form the general point at the actual delta* and
   278	     verify ord g<0 before using Prop.6.1.  Factor every leading polynomial.
   279	       A. One distinct g-root: output BRANCH A with the full T-root profile.
   280	       B. More than one distinct g-root: output BRANCH B with the full
   281	          multiplicity partition.
   282	     Apply only a case-proved coordinate transform and coefficient system.
   283	     If either is absent, return OPEN; a lower coefficient count is not a kill.
   284	  7. If only P is known, never relabel its radius as delta*.  Multiple roots
   285	     at radius r give delta*<=r only after checking that both belong to the
   286	     selected minor cluster; a one-root g profile gives no combined bound.
   287	     Output the supported branch plus OPEN.
   288	```
   289	
   290	For `(99,66)`, p.209 supplies `P`, not `R`, and asserts its row-specific A/B
   291	profiles.  Step 7 proves failure only in B.  For `(108,72)`, step 4 returns
   292	`OPEN[MINOR-RADIUS-108]`; §4.2 is the continuation once `R` exists.
