   333	  `(n,m,M2,V2,delta2,delta1;J)=(27,18,21,8,-1,0;X^4)` and says the earlier
   334	  method reduces to 10 coefficients (p.209 table and following sentence).
   335	- In alternative (ii), p.209 gives a Laurent transformation
