   344	
   345	### Final assertion and what Appendix II does not contain
   346	
   347	The last paragraph of p.211 says all other cases “can be computed directly as
   348	above” and concludes no counterexample through degree 100.  There is no
   349	printed computation for five of the six expanded p.202 rows, and no general
   350	numerical theorem is stated that eliminates them simultaneously.
   351	
   352	In particular, Appendix II contains:
   353	
   354	- no expression `H=L_1^u L_2^v` and no `L_1,L_2` split;
   355	- no new condition of the form `m | (...)`;
   356	- no new sign or ordering restriction on the `M_i` beyond using the listed
   357	  data and `m=-M_1`;
   358	- no all-level root-count rule.  The only explicit count partition is `2,2,6`
   359	  for the single transformed `(15,10,V2=3)` case;
   360	- no independent “second point at infinity” filter.  Section 6 identifies
   361	  `delta_s=-1` with more than one point at infinity in Corollary 6.1 (p.199),
   362	  and the Appendix uses the resulting minor-disc geometry, but does not turn
   363	  it into another pre-table scalar test;
   364	- no pre-table elimination of excess numerical rows.  Its opening premise is
   365	  already the p.202 table.
   366	
   367	## Source-only verdict for OPEN[MOH-PROGRAM]
   368	
   369	**Appendix II does not close OPEN[MOH-PROGRAM].**  It performs transformations,
   370	coefficient-count reductions, and one detailed case-specific contradiction
   371	*after* Moh's unexplained program has selected the six rows.  It cannot explain
   372	how the program discarded other tuples.
   373	
   374	The minor-disc pages expose two safe candidates to test against the census:
