+# Moh `(99,66)`: the radius-two cubic branches after `Omega`
+
+## Verdict first
+
+`MECHANICAL-CHECK`: PASS.  The manifest was generated from the lane receipt
+`xmodel/moh9966-branchB-sol56-20260903.run.v2`; no digest was retyped.  The
+initial `awk`/`sha256sum -c` check returned `OK` for all nine frozen inputs, and
+the independent driver recheck also returned `ok=true`.  The generated manifest
+is `box/moh9966B-20260903/charged-inputs.sha256`.
+
+The useful new result is:
+
+* `DERIVED-SOURCE / SATURATED-EMPTY`: the omitted radius-two cubic branch C,
+  in which the cubic has three simple roots and the `g` packets are `9+9+9`,
+  is impossible.  Moh's Propositions 3.2, 3.3, 4.1 and 6.1 force a degree-40
+  leading polynomial to vanish at least 14 times at each of three roots.
+  The exact reduced ideal has reduced basis `[1]` over three primes and over
+  `Q`; a five-term rational unit certificate is recorded below.
+* `REPRESENTATIVE[NECESSARY-ODE-FACE]`: branch B is not killed by that necessary
+  equation.  It has the exact family
+  `H=z^2(z+3a)`, `R=z^25(z+3a)^14(z-2a)`, `a != 0`.  This is a point of the
+  leading-face variety, not a point of Moh's omitted full coefficient variety
+  and not a Keller pair.
+* `SATURATED-EMPTY[CONTROL-ANSATZ]`: the driver independently reconstructs the
+  charged 14-unknown branch-A predecessor and again obtains `[1]`.  Its bridge
+  to Moh's unprinted ten-coefficient branch-A system remains unproved.
+
+Consequently **“no Keller pair with the `(99,66)` skeleton” is not
+`PROVED-HERE`**.  Its exact status here is
+
+```text
+OPEN[B-FULL-11-VARIABLE-LIFT]
+OPEN[A-PRINTED-10-VARIABLE-BRIDGE]
+OPEN[PRINCIPAL-MINOR-RADIUS: source does not prove that every split occurs at 2]
+```
+
+At a fixed radius-two place, the partitions `[3]`, `[2+1]`, `[1+1+1]` are
+exhaustive; the last is now excluded.  That is not global exhaustiveness of the
+principal-minor analysis.  In particular, the frozen minor-disc audit already
+keeps the actual `delta_2^*` separate from Moh's major radius `delta_2=1/3`.
+
+## 1. Source reading and page images
+
+The source is the frozen PDF
+`/tmp/jc2-lane.WhlLe3/inputs/moh1983_jram340_configurations_of_roots.pdf`.
+Printed page `p` is PDF page `p-139` (one-based).  The requested images are:
+
+| printed pages | PDF pages | named images |
+|---|---:|---|
+| 150--152 | 11--13 | `box/moh9966B-20260903/pages/moh_pp150_152_pdf-11.png`, `-12.png`, `-13.png` |
+| 207--211 | 68--72 | `box/moh9966B-20260903/pages/moh_pp207_211_pdf-68.png` through `-72.png` |
+
+Supporting pages used for the derivation were also rendered: printed 159, 162,
+164, 170--171, 191--195, and 202 appear under the same `pages/` directory as
+`moh_p159_pdf20.png`, `moh_p162_pdf23.png`, `moh_p164_pdf25.png`,
+`moh_pp170_171_pdf-31.png`, `-32.png`, `moh_pp191_195_pdf-52.png` through
+`-56.png`, and `moh_p202_pdf63.png`.
+
+`SOURCE-READ`, pp.150--152.  Moh defines
+
+```text
+d_1=n, d_{j+1}=gcd(n,M_1,...,M_j),
+q_1=M_1, q_j=M_j-M_{j-1},
+lambda_j=sum_{i<=j} q_i d_i, mu_j=lambda_j/d_j.
+```
+
+For `M=(-66,77,97)` this gives
+
+```text
+d=(99,33,11,1), q=(-66,143,20),
+lambda=(-6534,-1815,-1595), mu=(-66,-55,-145).
+```
+
+Lemma 2.1 gives the Keller terminal index `e=n-1=98`.  Proposition 2.2,
+including its specialization statement, gives monic
+`deg_y T_2^psi=55` and `deg_y T_3^psi=145`, because `77,97<98`.
+
+`SOURCE-READ`, pp.194--195 and 202.  Here `d_3=11`, `v_3=8`, and
+`u_3=d_3-v_3=3`.  The top homogeneous split is therefore
+
+```text
+g_99 = [Y^3(Y-kappa X)^8]^9,
+f_66 = [Y^3(Y-kappa X)^8]^6,
+```
+
+after a linear normalization of the two directions.  Proposition 6.2 gives
+minor/major counts
+
+```text
+             g       f=T_1^psi       T_2^psi
+minor       27           18              15
+major       72           48              40.
+```
+
+The p.202 row gives `V_2=V_3=8`; Definition 5.1 gives the **major** radii
+`(delta_1,delta_2,delta_3)=(4/9,1/3,-1)`.  These are not the actual combined
+minor radius `delta_2^*`.
+
+`SOURCE-READ`, pp.207--211.  Page 207 says only that the first three exceptional
+rows have `u_3=1` and are descended with Propositions 6.3--6.4.  Thus that
+automatic descent does not cover `(99,66)`, whose `u_3=3`.  Page 209 states
+
+```text
+sigma=a_{-1}t^-1+a_0+a_1t+pi t^2,
+g(sigma)=g_sigma(pi)t^-18+...,
+```
+
+and asserts that `g_sigma` is a power of a linear polynomial or the ninth power
+of a cubic with precisely two roots.  For the latter it prints exactly
+
+```text
+Omega: X -> x^-1,
+       Y -> a_0+a_1*x+a_2*x^2+y*x^3,
+Omega(f)       = x^6 y^18 + ...,
+Omega(g)       = x^9 y^27 + ...,
+Omega(T_2^psi) = x^5 y^15 + ...,
+Omega(T_3^psi) = x^15 y^40 + ...,
+J(Omega(f),Omega(g))=x.
+```
+
+The first sentence of p.210 says that solutions in `k<<x^-1>>` and
+`k<<y^-1>>`, treated by a modified method, reduce the computation to 11
+variables.  It names neither those variables nor their monomial support nor
+their equations.  The displayed computation on pp.210--211 instead concerns
+the different row `(15,10,11,3)`.  The blanket final sentence is not an
+exhibited `(99,66)` computation.
+
+## 2. Why the four printed corners are forced
+
+Put `t=x` after `X=t^-1`.  Evaluation on the radius-two probe is the exact
+identity
+
+```text
+Omega(P)(t,(pi-a_2)/t)
+  = P(t^-1,a_0+a_1*t+pi*t^2).
+```
+
+Thus a new-coordinate monomial `x^e y^k` has probe weight `e-k`.  Proposition
+6.1 (pp.191--193) applies because `ord g(sigma)=-18<0`: the same probe is a
+distribution detector for `g,T_1^psi=f,T_2^psi`.  Their degrees have gcd 11,
+and their local degrees are `27,18,15`, so Definition 3.1 gives, for a monic
+cubic `H`,
+
+```text
+g(sigma)   = H(pi)^9 t^-18+...,
+f(sigma)   = H(pi)^6 t^-12+...,
+T_2(sigma) = H(pi)^5 t^-10+....
+```
+
+This derives `deg H=3`.  A `[2+1]` factorization of `H` consequently gives
+`18+9` roots of `g` in the two at-level packets.  Since two `g` roots then
+separate at radius 2, only `delta_2^* <= 2` follows; equality or attainment for
+the combined product is not inferred.
+
+At the top direction, a degree-`D` polynomial with `r` minor factors contributes
+the Newton face
+
+```text
+x^(4r-D) y^r (x^4 y-kappa)^(D-r).
+```
+
+For `(D,r)=(66,18),(99,27),(55,15)` the corner exponent `4r-D` is respectively
+`6,9,5`.  Proposition 4.6 supplies the top form of `T_3`: if
+`p=Y^3(Y-kappa X)^8`, it is `p^13 Y(Y-kappa X)`, hence the minor/major counts
+are `40,105`, and `4*40-145=15`.  This derives all four printed exponent pairs,
+not merely their numerical pattern.
+
+For branch B translate the double root to zero and write
+`H(z)=z^2(z+3a)`, `z=xy`, `a!=0`.  The radius-two faces are
+
+```text
+F_2  = y^12 (xy+3a)^6,
+G_2  = y^18 (xy+3a)^9,
+T2_2 = y^10 (xy+3a)^5.
+```
+
+The derived `T3_2` appears in Section 4.  These faces have lower `x`-exponent
+zero and their upper endpoints are the printed `x^6y^18`, `x^9y^27`, and
+`x^5y^15`.
+
+For comparison, selecting one root in branch C with
+`H=z(z-d_1)(z-d_2)` gives Laurent faces
+
+```text
+x^-6 y^6 (xy-d_1)^6(xy-d_2)^6,
+x^-9 y^9 (xy-d_1)^9(xy-d_2)^9,
+x^-5 y^5 (xy-d_1)^5(xy-d_2)^5.
+```
+
+Their upper endpoints are still the three printed monomials.  Therefore those
+monomials alone do not exclude C, and one must not silently assume that every
+`Omega(P)` is polynomial.
+
+Finally, the coordinate determinant is
+
+```text
+det D(X,Y)/D(x,y) = det D(x^-1,a_0+a_1x+a_2x^2+x^3y)/D(x,y) = -x.
+```
+
+If the original constant is `J(f,g)=c`, then
+`J(Omega f,Omega g)=-c*x`; Moh's displayed `+x` fixes `c=-1` (or uses the
+equivalent sign normalization).  The driver checks this orientation and the
+positive controls `J(x^2/2,y)=x`, `J(x^5/5,y)=x^4`.
+
+## 3. Shape from old-coordinate polynomiality
+
+Let `P(X,Y)=sum_{i+j<=D} p_ij X^iY^j`.  Its literal transform is
+
+```text
+Omega(P)=sum p_ij x^-i(a_0+a_1x+a_2x^2+x^3y)^j.                 (3.1)
+```
+
+Conversely, on a monomial,
+
+```text
+Omega^-1(x^e y^k)
+ = X^(k-e) [X^2(Y-a_0)-a_1X-a_2]^k.                            (3.2)
+```
+
+Equations (3.1)--(3.2), not a guessed polygon, are the exact polynomiality
+test: negative `X` powers and terms of total degree greater than `D` must cancel
+after coefficients with the same image are combined.  A single old monomial
+can only produce
+
+```text
+0<=k<=D,             4k-D <= e <= 2D+k,
+```
+
+but membership in this envelope is not sufficient, because inverse-image
+coefficients are correlated.
+
+Combining the top and radius-two weights gives the following useful maximal
+envelopes.  In branch B, with the polynomial lower face justified by the
+`2+1` root counts,
+
+```text
+F:  max(0,k-12,4k-66)  <= e <= 132+k, 0<=k<=66;
+G:  max(0,k-18,4k-99)  <= e <= 198+k, 0<=k<=99;
+T2: max(0,k-10,4k-55)  <= e <= 110+k, 0<=k<=55;
+T3: max(0,k-25,4k-145) <= e <= 290+k, 0<=k<=145.
+```
+
+They contain `6109,13645,4261,29116` lattice sites.  In branch C the first
+floors are `-6,-9,-5`, giving `6166,13771,4301` sites for `F,G,T2`.  These are
+`COUNTING-BOUND` support-site counts, never independent-variable counts.
+
+A more stringent calculation shows exactly why the printed information does
+not yield Moh's 11.  In a straightened two-arc **slice**, define
+
+```text
+K(x,w)=x^11 h(x^-1,w/x)=sum_i x^i P_i(w),  deg P_i<=11-i.
+```
+
+The minor order `ord h=-2` requires `i+3j>=9` at `w=0`; the major order
+`ord h=-1/3` requires `3i+4j>=32` at `w=1`.  Hence
+
+```text
+w^3(w-1)^8,
+x^3 w^2(w-1)^6, x^4 w^2(w-1)^5,
+x^6 w(w-1)^4, x^7 w(w-1)^3, x^8 w(w-1)^2,
+x^9(w-1)^2, x^10(w-1), x^11                              (3.3)
+```
+
+is a basis: dimension 9, or eight free coefficients after monicity.  The
+minor initial cubic is
+`pi^3+c_3 pi^2+c_6 pi+c_9`.  Translating its double root to zero gives
+`c_6=c_9=0`; requiring `Omega(h)` polynomial then gives `c_10=0`.  Five
+coefficients remain, with
+
+```text
+Omega(h)=x*y^3(x^4y-1)^8
+ +c_3*y^2(x^4y-1)^6+c_4*x*y^2(x^4y-1)^5
+ +c_7*y(x^4y-1)^3+c_8*x*y(x^4y-1)^2+c_11.                  (3.4)
+```
+
+`TYPE[GAUGE-SLICE]`: (3.3)--(3.4) are rigorous after straightening the two
+arcs, but p.209 retains `a_0,a_1,a_2` and does not prove that the straightening
+preserves both filtrations and old-coordinate polynomiality.  Thus (3.4) is
+not promoted as Moh's literal ansatz.
+
+The same slice leaves dimensions `103` and `217` for the separate degree-66
+and degree-99 polynomial shapes after `Omega`-polynomiality.  Even fixing all
+three boundary faces leaves strict-interior perturbation spaces of dimensions
+`68` and `165`.  These 233 directions need not satisfy the approximate-root
+relations or the Jacobian, but they prove that the stated order and inverse
+conditions alone do not produce 11 coefficients.  Before any constraints, the
+ordinary monic total-degree arrays have `2277+5049=7326` free coefficients.
+Moh prints 7348 on p.207; this report does not silently identify his counting
+convention with the present monic gauge.
+
+The differing assumption is now precise: Moh additionally invokes an
+unprinted, modified simultaneous root/approximate-root reduction in both
+Laurent fields.  Reconstructing only from his four corners would invent the
+missing h-adic supports.
+
+## 4. The Jacobian face equation and branch B
+
+`DERIVED-SOURCE`.  Proposition 3.2 gives
+
+```text
+deg_y (T_3^psi)_f = -mu_3+M_3 = 145+97 = 242.
+```
+
+Proposition 3.3 applies at this same radius-two place: `M_2,M_3<=e=98`, the
+probe detects `g,f,T_2`, and `ord g<0`.  Consequently
+
+```text
+(T_3^psi)_f(sigma)=c_f H(pi)^22 t^-44+...,  c_f!=0.
+```
+
+This is the formal `f`-derivative, not `T_3` itself, and it is not moved to a
+child place.  From Moh's `x^15y^40` corner write
+
+```text
+T_3^psi(sigma)=R(pi)t^-25+...,  deg R=40.
+```
+
+Proposition 4.1 applied to `(T_3^psi,g)` and the equality
+`J(T_3^psi,g)=(T_3^psi)_f J(f,g)` now gives, after absorbing a nonzero scalar,
+
+```text
+                 2 H R' - 25 H' R = k H^14,   k!=0.          (4.1)
+```
+
+At a root of `H` of multiplicity `m`, let `r` be its multiplicity in `R`.
+Unless `2r=25m`, comparison in (4.1) gives `r=13m+1`.  For branch B the simple
+root therefore has `r=14`.  At the double root the nonresonant `r=27` would
+already make `deg R>=41`, so resonance is forced and `r=25`.  Hence
+
+```text
+H=z^2(z+3a), R=H^12 q,
+q=z^4+q_3z^3+q_2z^2+q_1z+q_0, a!=0,
+2Hq'-H'q-kH^2=0.                                             (4.2)
+```
+
+The six raw coefficients of (4.2) are
+
+```text
+5-k,
+3(-2ak+6a+q_3),
+-9a^2k+12aq_3+q_2,
+6aq_2-q_1,
+-3q_0,
+-6aq_0.
+```
+
+The last is twice `a` times the preceding generator.  The declared ring is
+`Q[a,k,q3,q2,q1,q0,T]`; saturation by `a*k` is represented exactly by adjoining
+`T*a*k-1` and extracting the extended ideal in that ring.
+
+| field | generators incl. wrapper | reduced-basis size | result |
+|---|---:|---:|---|
+| `F_32003` | 6 | 9 | `NONUNIT` |
+| `F_32009` | 6 | 9 | `NONUNIT` |
+| `F_32027` | 6 | 9 | `NONUNIT` |
+| `Q` | 6 | 9 | `NONUNIT` |
+
+The exact solution family is
+
+```text
+k=5, q_3=4a, q_2=-3a^2, q_1=-18a^3, q_0=0,
+q=z(z-2a)(z+3a)^2, T=(5a)^-1.
+```
+
+At `a=1`, direct symbolic substitution gives zero remainder in (4.1):
+
+```text
+H=z^2(z+3), R=z^25(z+3)^14(z-2).
+```
+
+The corresponding bivariate faces are
+
+```text
+T3_2=y^25(xy+3)^14(xy-2), G_2=y^18(xy+3)^9,
+J(T3_2,G_2)=45*x*y^44*(xy+3)^22.
+```
+
+This directly checks the Jacobian-derived face identity.  It is explicitly
+**not** a check of `J(Omega(f),Omega(g))=x`, because no full `F,G` lift has been
+constructed.  Branch B therefore `SURVIVES[NECESSARY-ODE]` but remains
+`OPEN[B-FULL-11-VARIABLE-LIFT]`, not `SURVIVES[KELLER]`.
+
+## 5. Branch C: exact exclusion and saturation certificate
+
+If `H` has three simple roots, resonance is impossible because `2r=25` has no
+integer solution.  Equation (4.1) forces multiplicity 14 at each root, hence
+`deg R>=42`, contradicting `deg R=40`.  This is already a direct branch-C kill.
+
+For a coefficient-system check, work on the squarefree stratum.  If
+`R=H^jR_j`, then (4.1) becomes
+
+```text
+2H R_j' +(2j-25)H'R_j = k H^(14-j).
+```
+
+For `j=0,...,12`, reduction modulo `H` shows `H|R_j`: the integers
+`2j-25` are nonzero and `H'` is a unit modulo squarefree `H`.  Thus
+`R=H^13L`, where `L` is monic linear, and the remaining necessary equation is
+
+```text
+H'L+2HL'-kH=0.                                                (5.1)
+```
+
+Normalize `H=z(z-a)(z-b)`, `L=z+ell`.  The four coefficients of (5.1) are
+
+```text
+f1=5-k,
+f2=(k-4)(a+b)+3ell,
+f3=(3-k)ab-2(a+b)ell,
+f4=ab ell.
+```
+
+The ring is `Q[a,b,ell,k,T]`; the squarefree/nonzero stratum is selected by
+`f5=T*ab(a-b)k-1`.  Singular returns `[1]` in each of `F_32003`, `F_32009`,
+`F_32027`, and `Q`, in 0.016--0.019 seconds per run.  Each run passed the empty
+wrapper, nonempty wrapper, and unsaturated-nonunit controls.
+
+`CERTIFICATE-SIZE`: one polynomial in the reduced basis.  An independently
+expanded rational certificate has five summands and maximum multiplier total
+degree 7.  Put `s=a+b`, `p=ab`, `d=a-b`; then
+
+```text
+m1=T*d*k*(p/2-ell*s), m2=-T*d*k*ell, m3=-T*d*k/2,
+m4=3*T^2*d^2*k^2*ell, m5=-3*T*d*k*ell^2-1,
+1 = m1*f1+m2*f2+m3*f3+m4*f4+m5*f5.
+```
+
+The unsaturated equations deliberately retain the degeneration
+`a=b=ell=0,k=5`, so the unit result is not an artifact of an already-unit raw
+ideal.  Conceptually, (5.1) evaluated at each simple root says `H'(r)L(r)=0`;
+a monic linear polynomial cannot vanish at three distinct roots.  Therefore
+branch C is `SATURATED-EMPTY`, not merely a counting bound.
+
+## 6. Branch-A control
+
+The self-contained control rebuilds the charged predecessor in
+
+```text
+Q[h_0_8,...,h_0_0,bp,bq,br,bs,c,T]
+```
+
+with 14 unknowns excluding `T`:
+
+```text
+h=y^8(y-x)+sum_{j=0}^8 h_0_j y^j,
+A=(h-h|_{y=0})/y, beta=bp*A+bq*y+br*x+bs,
+alpha=quotient_y(beta^2,h),
+f=h^2+2beta, g=h^3+3beta*h+(3/2)alpha.
+```
+
+H-adic extraction of `J(f,g)-c*x^4` gives the charged 29 equations; raw
+expansion gives 36, an extraction-method difference rather than a different
+ansatz.  In both forms the coefficient `-c` occurs.  After adjoining `T*c-1`,
+
+```text
+1=-(T*c-1)-T*(-c).
+```
+
+Thus the certificate has two summands and maximum multiplier degree 1.  All
+three primes and `Q` return `[1]` in under 0.020 seconds and pass the wrapper
+controls.  This exactly reproduces the charged 14-unknown predecessor result.
+
+`TYPE[CONTROL-ONLY]`: Moh does not print the map from every linear-power
+candidate to this 14-unknown predecessor or to his stated ten coefficients.
+The immediate `-c` also shows that this test is a structural ansatz check, not
+the missing computation.  It is not promoted to a proof that branch A itself
+is empty.
+
+## 7. What the exact full system would require
+
+There is a finite first-principles system, but it is not Moh's missing
+11-variable system.  Start with the 7326 old-coordinate coefficients in the
+two monic total-degree arrays and parameters `a_0,a_1,a_2`.  Form `F,G` by
+(3.1); impose all inverse polynomiality relations from (3.2), both Newton
+faces, the universal approximate-root definitions of `T_2^psi,T_3^psi`, and
+every coefficient of
+
+```text
+J(F,G)+c*x=0, c!=0, T*c-1=0
+```
+
+(with the sign convention above).  One must then prove and apply the
+filtration-preserving h-adic/gauge eliminations that map this system to eleven
+variables.  Pp.209--210 omit precisely those eliminations and the resulting
+support.  Saturating an invented eleven-monomial slice would not answer the
+question.
+
+The reduced ODE systems are exact necessary images of that full Jacobian
+system.  Therefore their logical force is asymmetric: emptiness of C lifts to
+the full C branch because every C candidate maps into (5.1), while nonemptiness
+of B does not lift backward without solving all omitted coefficient equations.
+
+There is a second exhaustiveness gap.  P.209 asserts the radius-two description
+but does not prove that principal minor roots cannot first split at another
+admissible radius.  As external corroboration, Yansong Xu, *Intersection
+Numbers and Split of Minor Roots*, arXiv:1604.07683v4, Section 8, proves the
+three-root exclusion at radius 2 but records a possible `delta=5/2` split and
+describes `(99,66)` as open.  This is `EXTERNAL-CORROBORATION`, not part of the
+frozen-source proof.
+
+## 8. Reproduction and FALLACY-v2 audit
+
+Run serially (one core, 120-second timeout per Singular call):
+
+```text
+python3 box/moh9966B-20260903/moh9966B_driver.py
+```
+
+Primary artifacts are
+
+```text
+box/moh9966B-20260903/moh9966B_driver.py
+box/moh9966B-20260903/moh9966B_results.json
+box/moh9966B-20260903/systems/*.sing
+box/moh9966B-20260903/logs/*.log
+box/moh9966B-20260903/artifacts.sha256
+```
+
+Measured software was Python 3, SymPy 1.12, and Singular 4.3.2.  The driver
+declares every ring and generator order, records the map into each Singular
+ring, and uses the Rabinowitsch extended ideal rather than an unchecked
+`sat()` return wrapper.  Both positive and negative controls are run.  Prime
+marks are nowhere interpreted as derivatives; derivatives are written
+explicitly.
+
+FALLACY-v2: the major radii, radius-two place, and actual combined minor radius
+remain distinct; at-level packet counts do not assert deeper attainment.  The
+branch-B point is typed `REPRESENTATIVE[NECESSARY-ODE-FACE]`, never
+`FULL_ACTUAL_EXIT` or a Keller witness.  No new exit-price assertion is made,
+so no `charge_basis` line is licensed.
+
+<!-- BODY-END -->

diff --git a/box/moh9966B-20260903/moh9966B_driver.py b/box/moh9966B-20260903/moh9966B_driver.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..252702147ec26257857d88273ad5e491d54b6349
--- /dev/null
+++ b/box/moh9966B-20260903/moh9966B_driver.py
@@ -0,0 +1,643 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Reproducible checks for Moh's (99,66) radius-two B/C analysis.
+
+This driver deliberately distinguishes three systems:
+
+* A is the charged 14-unknown A/B predecessor control for Moh's transformed
+  linear-power row.  It is rebuilt here without importing the earlier,
+  uncharged helper.
+* B is the necessary leading-coefficient ODE on the two-root cubic stratum.
+* C is a necessary reduced consequence of the same ODE on the squarefree
+  cubic stratum.
+
+The B system is not Moh's omitted eleven-variable full coefficient system.
+Its nonempty result must therefore not be read as a Keller-pair witness.
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import hashlib
+import json
+import math
+import re
+import shutil
+import subprocess
+import time
+from pathlib import Path
+
+import sympy as sp
+
+
+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
+OUT = ROOT / "box" / "moh9966B-20260903"
+SYSTEMS_DIR = OUT / "systems"
+LOGS_DIR = OUT / "logs"
+RESULT_PATH = OUT / "moh9966B_results.json"
+RECEIPT = ROOT / "xmodel" / "moh9966-branchB-sol56-20260903.run.v2"
+PRIMES = (32003, 32009, 32027)
+CHARACTERISTICS = PRIMES + (0,)
+
+
+def sha256_file(path: Path) -> str:
+    digest = hashlib.sha256()
+    with path.open("rb") as handle:
+        for chunk in iter(lambda: handle.read(1 << 20), b""):
+            digest.update(chunk)
+    return digest.hexdigest()
+
+
+def receipt_manifest_check() -> dict:
+    """Read both filenames and hashes from the receipt; retype neither."""
+    fields: dict[str, str] = {}
+    for line in RECEIPT.read_text().splitlines():
+        if "=" in line:
+            key, value = line.split("=", 1)
+            fields[key] = value
+    input_dir = Path(fields["lane_inputs_dir"])
+    count = int(fields["charged_inputs"])
+    rows = []
+    for index in range(1, count + 1):
+        basename = fields[f"charged_input_{index}_basename"]
+        expected = fields[f"charged_input_{index}_sha256"]
+        path = input_dir / basename
+        got = sha256_file(path) if path.is_file() else None
+        rows.append(
+            {
+                "index": index,
+                "basename": basename,
+                "path": str(path),
+                "expected": expected,
+                "got": got,
+                "ok": got == expected,
+            }
+        )
+    manifest_path = OUT / "charged-inputs.sha256"
+    manifest_path.write_text(
+        "".join(f"{row['expected']}  {row['path']}\n" for row in rows)
+    )
+    return {
+        "method": "receipt fields parsed mechanically; SHA-256 recomputed",
+        "receipt": str(RECEIPT),
+        "input_dir": str(input_dir),
+        "ok": all(row["ok"] for row in rows),
+        "rows": rows,
+        "manifest": str(manifest_path.relative_to(ROOT)),
+    }
+
+
+def jacobian(first: sp.Expr, second: sp.Expr, x: sp.Symbol, y: sp.Symbol) -> sp.Expr:
+    return sp.expand(
+        sp.diff(first, x) * sp.diff(second, y)
+        - sp.diff(first, y) * sp.diff(second, x)
+    )
+
+
+def singular_expr(expr: sp.Expr) -> str:
+    numerator, denominator = sp.fraction(sp.together(sp.expand(expr)))
+    numerator = sp.expand(numerator)
+    denominator = sp.expand(denominator)
+    if denominator == 1:
+        text = str(numerator)
+    elif denominator == -1:
+        text = str(-numerator)
+    else:
+        text = f"({numerator})/({denominator})"
+    return text.replace("**", "^")
+
+
+def coefficient_equations(poly: sp.Expr, x: sp.Symbol, y: sp.Symbol) -> list[sp.Expr]:
+    return [sp.expand(value) for value in sp.Poly(sp.expand(poly), x, y).coeffs() if value != 0]
+
+
+def hadic_jacobian_equations(
+    h: sp.Expr,
+    low_terms: list[tuple[sp.Expr, int]],
+    high_terms: list[tuple[sp.Expr, int]],
+    c: sp.Symbol,
+    x_power: int,
+    x: sp.Symbol,
+    y: sp.Symbol,
+) -> tuple[list[sp.Expr], list[int]]:
+    """Extract J(low,high) by powers of a monic polynomial h.
+
+    A term is represented as (coefficient, h-exponent).  Euclidean division
+    in Q(parameters,x)[y] carries every quotient to the next h-adic level.
+    """
+    by_power: dict[int, sp.Expr] = {}
+    for aa, r_power in low_terms:
+        for bb, s_power in high_terms:
+            value = jacobian(aa, bb, x, y)
+            if value != 0:
+                by_power[r_power + s_power] = by_power.get(r_power + s_power, 0) + value
+            value = (
+                s_power * bb * jacobian(aa, h, x, y)
+                + r_power * aa * jacobian(h, bb, x, y)
+            )
+            if value != 0:
+                level = r_power + s_power - 1
+                by_power[level] = by_power.get(level, 0) + value
+
+    by_power.setdefault(0, sp.Integer(0))
+    level = 0
+    largest = max(by_power)
+    while level <= largest:
+        remainder = sp.expand(by_power.get(level, 0))
+        if remainder != 0:
+            quotient, residue = sp.div(sp.Poly(remainder, y), sp.Poly(h, y), y)
+            by_power[level] = sp.expand(residue.as_expr())
+            if quotient != 0:
+                by_power[level + 1] = by_power.get(level + 1, 0) + sp.expand(quotient.as_expr())
+                largest = max(largest, level + 1)
+        level += 1
+
+    by_power[0] = sp.expand(by_power[0] - c * x**x_power)
+    equations: list[sp.Expr] = []
+    nonzero_levels: list[int] = []
+    for level in sorted(by_power):
+        remainder = sp.expand(by_power[level])
+        if remainder == 0:
+            continue
+        nonzero_levels.append(level)
+        equations.extend(coefficient_equations(remainder, x, y))
+    return equations, nonzero_levels
+
+
+def branch_a_predecessor() -> dict:
+    """Rebuild the charged 13-shape-variable plus c predecessor."""
+    x, y = sp.symbols("x y")
+    h_parameters = list(
+        sp.symbols("h_0_8 h_0_7 h_0_6 h_0_5 h_0_4 h_0_3 h_0_2 h_0_1 h_0_0")
+    )
+    h = y**8 * (y - x)
+    for parameter, y_power in zip(h_parameters, range(8, -1, -1)):
+        h += parameter * y**y_power
+    bp, bq, br, bs, c, T = sp.symbols("bp bq br bs c T")
+    A = sp.cancel((h - h.subs(y, 0)) / y)
+    beta = sp.expand(bp * A + bq * y + br * x + bs)
+    quotient, _ = sp.div(sp.Poly(sp.expand(beta**2), y), sp.Poly(h, y), y)
+    alpha = sp.expand(quotient.as_expr())
+    low_terms = [(sp.Integer(1), 2), (2 * beta, 0)]
+    high_terms = [
+        (sp.Integer(1), 3),
+        (3 * beta, 1),
+        (sp.Rational(3, 2) * alpha, 0),
+    ]
+    equations, levels = hadic_jacobian_equations(
+        h, low_terms, high_terms, c, 4, x, y
+    )
+    raw_f = sp.expand(h**2 + 2 * beta)
+    raw_g = sp.expand(h**3 + 3 * beta * h + sp.Rational(3, 2) * alpha)
+    raw_equations = coefficient_equations(jacobian(raw_f, raw_g, x, y) - c * x**4, x, y)
+    assert len(equations) == 29
+    assert len(raw_equations) == 36
+    assert equations[0] == -c
+    parameters = h_parameters + [bp, bq, br, bs, c]
+    return {
+        "name": "A_CONTROL_PREDECESSOR",
+        "parameters": parameters,
+        "T": T,
+        "factor": c,
+        "equations": equations,
+        "levels": levels,
+        "raw_equation_count": len(raw_equations),
+        "certificate": "1 = -(T*c-1) - T*(-c)",
+        "certificate_terms": 2,
+        "certificate_max_multiplier_degree": 1,
+    }
+
+
+def branch_b_ode() -> dict:
+    z = sp.Symbol("z")
+    a, k, q3, q2, q1, q0, T = sp.symbols("a k q3 q2 q1 q0 T")
+    H = z**2 * (z + 3 * a)
+    q = z**4 + q3 * z**3 + q2 * z**2 + q1 * z + q0
+    ode = sp.expand(2 * H * sp.diff(q, z) - sp.diff(H, z) * q - k * H**2)
+    raw = [sp.expand(ode.coeff(z, degree)) for degree in range(6, 0, -1)]
+    assert raw[-1] == sp.expand(2 * a * raw[-2])
+    equations = raw[:-1]
+
+    witness = {a: 1, k: 5, q3: 4, q2: -3, q1: -18, q0: 0, T: sp.Rational(1, 5)}
+    H_w = sp.expand(H.subs(witness))
+    q_w = sp.expand(q.subs(witness))
+    R_w = sp.expand(H_w**12 * q_w)
+    full_ode = sp.expand(2 * H_w * sp.diff(R_w, z) - 25 * sp.diff(H_w, z) * R_w - 5 * H_w**14)
+    assert full_ode == 0
+    assert all(sp.expand(eq.subs(witness)) == 0 for eq in equations)
+
+    x, y = sp.symbols("x y")
+    zxy = x * y
+    t3_face = y**25 * (zxy + 3) ** 14 * (zxy - 2)
+    g_face = y**18 * (zxy + 3) ** 9
+    face_jac = sp.factor(jacobian(t3_face, g_face, x, y))
+    expected_face_jac = 45 * x * y**44 * (zxy + 3) ** 22
+    assert sp.expand(face_jac - expected_face_jac) == 0
+
+    return {
+        "name": "B_TWO_ROOT_REDUCED_ODE",
+        "parameters": [a, k, q3, q2, q1, q0],
+        "T": T,
+        "factor": a * k,
+        "equations": equations,
+        "raw_equations": raw,
+        "dropped_redundant": str(sp.Eq(raw[-1], 2 * a * raw[-2])),
+        "witness": {
+            "a": 1,
+            "k": 5,
+            "q3": 4,
+            "q2": -3,
+            "q1": -18,
+            "q0": 0,
+            "T": "1/5",
+            "H": str(H_w),
+            "q": str(sp.factor(q_w)),
+            "R": str(sp.factor(R_w)),
+            "full_ode_remainder": str(full_ode),
+            "bivariate_face_jacobian": str(face_jac),
+            "bivariate_face_jacobian_expected": str(expected_face_jac),
+            "type": "REPRESENTATIVE[NECESSARY-ODE-FACE], not a Keller pair",
+        },
+    }
+
+
+def branch_c_consequence() -> dict:
+    z = sp.Symbol("z")
+    a, b, ell, k, T = sp.symbols("a b ell k T")
+    H = z * (z - a) * (z - b)
+    L = z + ell
+    consequence = sp.expand(sp.diff(H, z) * L + 2 * H * sp.diff(L, z) - k * H)
+    equations = [sp.expand(consequence.coeff(z, degree)) for degree in range(3, -1, -1)]
+
+    symmetric_sum = a + b
+    symmetric_product = a * b
+    difference = a - b
+    f1, f2, f3, f4 = equations
+    f5 = T * symmetric_product * difference * k - 1
+    multipliers = [
+        T * difference * k * (symmetric_product / 2 - ell * symmetric_sum),
+        -T * difference * k * ell,
+        -T * difference * k / 2,
+        3 * T**2 * difference**2 * k**2 * ell,
+        -3 * T * difference * k * ell**2 - 1,
+    ]
+    certificate_remainder = sp.expand(
+        multipliers[0] * f1
+        + multipliers[1] * f2
+        + multipliers[2] * f3
+        + multipliers[3] * f4
+        + multipliers[4] * f5
+        - 1
+    )
+    assert certificate_remainder == 0
+    degenerate = {a: 0, b: 0, ell: 0, k: 5}
+    assert all(sp.expand(eq.subs(degenerate)) == 0 for eq in equations)
+    return {
+        "name": "C_THREE_SIMPLE_REDUCED_CONSEQUENCE",
+        "parameters": [a, b, ell, k],
+        "T": T,
+        "factor": a * b * (a - b) * k,
+        "equations": equations,
+        "certificate": {
+            "identity_remainder": str(certificate_remainder),
+            "terms": 5,
+            "max_multiplier_total_degree": max(
+                sp.Poly(multiplier, a, b, ell, k, T).total_degree()
+                for multiplier in multipliers
+            ),
+            "multipliers": [str(value) for value in multipliers],
+        },
+        "unsaturated_degenerate_point": {"a": 0, "b": 0, "ell": 0, "k": 5},
+    }
+
+
+def clean_name(symbol: sp.Symbol) -> str:
+    name = re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9_]+", "_", str(symbol)).strip("_")
+    return name if name and not name[0].isdigit() else f"v{name}"
+
+
+def singular_script(spec: dict, characteristic: int) -> tuple[str, dict[sp.Symbol, sp.Symbol]]:
+    parameters = list(spec["parameters"])
+    T = spec["T"]
+    symbols = parameters + [T]
+    names: list[str] = []
+    rename: dict[sp.Symbol, sp.Symbol] = {}
+    for symbol in symbols:
+        base = clean_name(symbol)
+        name = base
+        suffix = 1
+        while name in names:
+            suffix += 1
+            name = f"{base}_{suffix}"
+        names.append(name)
+        rename[symbol] = sp.Symbol(name)
+    equations = [sp.expand(eq.subs(rename)) for eq in spec["equations"]]
+    factor = sp.expand(spec["factor"].subs(rename))
+    t_name = rename[T]
+
+    # Explicit nonempty wrapper-control points; they test only the wrapper.
+    if spec["name"].startswith("C_"):
+        control_values = {"a": "1", "b": "2", "k": "1", "T": "-1/2"}
+    else:
+        first_name = clean_name(parameters[0])
+        control_values = {first_name: "1", "T": "1"}
+        if "k" in names:
+            control_values["k"] = "1"
+        if spec["name"].startswith("A_"):
+            control_values = {"c": "1", "T": "1"}
+    control_generators = [f"{name}-({value})" for name, value in control_values.items()]
+
+    equation_text = ",\n  ".join(singular_expr(eq) for eq in equations)
+    main_generators = equation_text + f",\n  {t_name}*({singular_expr(factor)})-1"
+    text = f"""// {spec['name']}; characteristic {characteristic}
+ring R={characteristic},({','.join(names)}),dp;
+option(redSB);
+print(\"RING_BEGIN\"); R; print(\"RING_END\");
+ideal CE={singular_expr(factor)},{t_name}*({singular_expr(factor)})-1;
+ideal GCE=std(CE);
+if (reduce(1,GCE)==0) {{ print(\"CONTROL_EMPTY_PASS\"); }} else {{ print(\"CONTROL_EMPTY_FAIL\"); }}
+ideal CN={','.join(control_generators)};
+ideal GCN=std(CN);
+if (reduce(1,GCN)!=0) {{ print(\"CONTROL_NONEMPTY_PASS\"); }} else {{ print(\"CONTROL_NONEMPTY_FAIL\"); }}
+ideal E=
+  {equation_text};
+ideal GU=std(E);
+if (reduce(1,GU)!=0) {{ print(\"UNSATURATED_NONUNIT_PASS\"); }} else {{ print(\"UNSATURATED_NONUNIT_FAIL\"); }}
+ideal I=
+  {main_generators};
+ideal G=std(I);
+print(\"GENERATOR_COUNT\"); size(E);
+print(\"EXTENDED_GENERATOR_COUNT\"); size(I);
+print(\"BASIS_SIZE\"); size(G);
+print(\"BASIS_BEGIN\"); G; print(\"BASIS_END\");
+if (reduce(1,G)==0) {{ print(\"MAIN_SATURATED_EMPTY\"); }} else {{ print(\"MAIN_NONUNIT\"); }}
+quit;
+"""
+    return text, rename
+
+
+def parse_singular_output(output: str) -> dict:
+    lines = [line.strip() for line in output.splitlines()]
+
+    def after(label: str) -> str | None:
+        try:
+            return lines[lines.index(label) + 1]
+        except (ValueError, IndexError):
+            return None
+
+    try:
+        begin = lines.index("BASIS_BEGIN") + 1
+        end = lines.index("BASIS_END")
+        basis = lines[begin:end]
+    except ValueError:
+        basis = []
+    if "MAIN_SATURATED_EMPTY" in lines:
+        verdict = "SATURATED-EMPTY"
+    elif "MAIN_NONUNIT" in lines:
+        verdict = "NONUNIT"
+    else:
+        verdict = "ERROR"
+    controls = {
+        "empty_wrapper": "CONTROL_EMPTY_PASS" in lines,
+        "nonempty_wrapper": "CONTROL_NONEMPTY_PASS" in lines,
+        "unsaturated_nonunit": "UNSATURATED_NONUNIT_PASS" in lines,
+    }
+    if not all(controls.values()):
+        verdict = "CONTROL-FAIL"
+    return {
+        "verdict": verdict,
+        "controls": controls,
+        "generator_count": after("GENERATOR_COUNT"),
+        "extended_generator_count": after("EXTENDED_GENERATOR_COUNT"),
+        "basis_size": after("BASIS_SIZE"),
+        "basis": basis,
+    }
+
+
+def run_system(spec: dict, characteristic: int, timeout_seconds: int = 120) -> dict:
+    label = "Q" if characteristic == 0 else str(characteristic)
+    stem = spec["name"].lower()
+    script_path = SYSTEMS_DIR / f"{stem}_{label}.sing"
+    log_path = LOGS_DIR / f"{stem}_{label}.log"
+    text, rename = singular_script(spec, characteristic)
+    script_path.write_text(text)
+    started = time.perf_counter()
+    try:
+        process = subprocess.run(
+            ["Singular", "-q", "--no-rc", str(script_path)],
+            capture_output=True,
+            text=True,
+            timeout=timeout_seconds,
+            check=False,
+        )
+        elapsed = time.perf_counter() - started
+        output = (process.stdout or "") + (process.stderr or "")
+        log_path.write_text(output)
+        record = parse_singular_output(output)
+        record.update({"returncode": process.returncode})
+        if process.returncode != 0:
+            record["verdict"] = "ERROR"
+    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as error:
+        elapsed = time.perf_counter() - started
+        stdout = error.stdout.decode(errors="replace") if isinstance(error.stdout, bytes) else (error.stdout or "")
+        stderr = error.stderr.decode(errors="replace") if isinstance(error.stderr, bytes) else (error.stderr or "")
+        output = stdout + stderr
+        log_path.write_text(output)
+        record = {"verdict": "TIMEOUT", "controls": {}, "basis": []}
+    record.update(
+        {
+            "characteristic": characteristic,
+            "elapsed_seconds": round(elapsed, 6),
+            "timeout_seconds": timeout_seconds,
+            "script": str(script_path.relative_to(ROOT)),
+            "log": str(log_path.relative_to(ROOT)),
+            "script_sha256": sha256_file(script_path),
+            "ring_variables": [str(rename[symbol]) for symbol in list(spec["parameters"]) + [spec["T"]]],
+        }
+    )
+    return record
+
+
+def ceil_fraction(numerator: int, denominator: int) -> int:
+    return -((-numerator) // denominator)
+
+
+def two_arc_dimension(D: int, minor_order: int, major_s_order: int, omega_polynomial: bool, strict: bool) -> int:
+    total = 0
+    bump = 1 if strict else 0
+    for x_degree in range(D + 1):
+        minor_vanish = max(0, ceil_fraction(minor_order + bump - x_degree, 3))
+        if omega_polynomial:
+            minor_vanish = max(
+                minor_vanish,
+                0,
+                ceil_fraction(D + bump - x_degree, 4),
+            )
+        major_vanish = max(0, ceil_fraction(major_s_order + bump - 3 * x_degree, 4))
+        cap = D - x_degree
+        total += max(0, cap - minor_vanish - major_vanish + 1)
+    return total
+
+
+def envelope_site_count(D: int, local_order: int, x_floor: int) -> int:
+    count = 0
+    for y_degree in range(D + 1):
+        lower = max(x_floor, y_degree + local_order, 4 * y_degree - D)
+        upper = 2 * D + y_degree
+        count += max(0, upper - lower + 1)
+    return count
+
+
+def shape_counts() -> dict:
+    h_rows = []
+    for x_degree in range(12):
+        cap = 11 - x_degree
+        minor_vanish = max(0, ceil_fraction(9 - x_degree, 3))
+        major_vanish = max(0, ceil_fraction(32 - 3 * x_degree, 4))
+        dimension = max(0, cap - minor_vanish - major_vanish + 1)
+        if dimension:
+            h_rows.append(
+                {
+                    "x_degree": x_degree,
+                    "w_degree_cap": cap,
+                    "w_zero_vanishing": minor_vanish,
+                    "w_one_vanishing": major_vanish,
+                    "dimension": dimension,
+                    "basis": f"x^{x_degree}*w^{minor_vanish}*(w-1)^{major_vanish}",
+                }
+            )
+    assert len(h_rows) == 9
+    raw_original = {
+        "f_monic_free": (67 * 68) // 2 - 1,
+        "g_monic_free": (100 * 101) // 2 - 1,
+    }
+    raw_original["total"] = raw_original["f_monic_free"] + raw_original["g_monic_free"]
+    result = {
+        "straightened_two_arc_h": {
+            "linear_dimension": sum(row["dimension"] for row in h_rows),
+            "affine_free_after_monic": sum(row["dimension"] for row in h_rows) - 1,
+            "rows": h_rows,
+            "branch_B_after_double_root_and_Omega_polynomiality_free": 5,
+            "surviving_indices": [3, 4, 7, 8, 11],
+            "type": "GAUGE-SLICE; literal a0,a1,a2 straightening is not proved by p.209",
+        },
+        "individual_P_spaces_in_zero_jet_slice": {
+            "without_Omega_polynomiality": {
+                "f": two_arc_dimension(66, 54, 192, False, False),
+                "g": two_arc_dimension(99, 81, 288, False, False),
+            },
+            "with_Omega_polynomiality": {
+                "f": two_arc_dimension(66, 54, 192, True, False),
+                "g": two_arc_dimension(99, 81, 288, True, False),
+            },
+            "strict_interior_preserving_all_faces": {
+                "f": two_arc_dimension(66, 54, 192, True, True),
+                "g": two_arc_dimension(99, 81, 288, True, True),
+            },
+            "type": "COUNTING-BOUND on separate f,g shapes, before approximate-root/Jacobian equations",
+        },
+        "maximal_envelope_support_sites": {
+            "B": {
+                "f": envelope_site_count(66, -12, 0),
+                "g": envelope_site_count(99, -18, 0),
+                "T2": envelope_site_count(55, -10, 0),
+                "T3": envelope_site_count(145, -25, 0),
+            },
+            "C": {
+                "f": envelope_site_count(66, -12, -6),
+                "g": envelope_site_count(99, -18, -9),
+                "T2": envelope_site_count(55, -10, -5),
+            },
+            "type": "support-site counts, not independent coefficient counts",
+        },
+        "raw_original_coefficient_count": raw_original,
+    }
+    assert result["individual_P_spaces_in_zero_jet_slice"]["with_Omega_polynomiality"] == {"f": 103, "g": 217}
+    assert result["individual_P_spaces_in_zero_jet_slice"]["strict_interior_preserving_all_faces"] == {"f": 68, "g": 165}
+    assert result["maximal_envelope_support_sites"]["B"] == {"f": 6109, "g": 13645, "T2": 4261, "T3": 29116}
+    assert result["maximal_envelope_support_sites"]["C"] == {"f": 6166, "g": 13771, "T2": 4301}
+    return result
+
+
+def orientation_controls() -> dict:
+    x, y, a0, a1, a2 = sp.symbols("x y a0 a1 a2")
+    old_x = x**-1
+    old_y = a0 + a1 * x + a2 * x**2 + x**3 * y
+    determinant = jacobian(old_x, old_y, x, y)
+    j_x = jacobian(x**2 / 2, y, x, y)
+    j_x4 = jacobian(x**5 / 5, y, x, y)
+    assert determinant == -x
+    assert j_x == x and j_x4 == x**4
+    return {
+        "det_DPhi": str(determinant),
+        "if_original_J_is_c": "J(Omega(f),Omega(g))=-c*x",
+        "Moh_J_equals_x_requires": "c=-1 (or an equivalent sign normalization)",
+        "positive_control_J_x": str(j_x),
+        "positive_control_J_x4": str(j_x4),
+    }
+
+
+def serializable_spec(spec: dict) -> dict:
+    result = {}
+    for key, value in spec.items():
+        if key in {"parameters"}:
+            result[key] = [str(item) for item in value]
+        elif key in {"T", "factor"}:
+            result[key] = str(value)
+        elif key in {"equations", "raw_equations"}:
+            result[key] = [str(item) for item in value]
+        else:
+            result[key] = value
+    return result
+
+
+def write_artifact_hashes() -> None:
+    paths = sorted(
+        path for path in OUT.rglob("*")
+        if path.is_file() and path.name != "artifacts.sha256"
+    )
+    (OUT / "artifacts.sha256").write_text(
+        "".join(f"{sha256_file(path)}  {path.relative_to(ROOT)}\n" for path in paths)
+    )
+
+
+def main() -> None:
+    if shutil.which("Singular") is None:
+        raise SystemExit("Singular is required")
+    OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    SYSTEMS_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    LOGS_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+
+    manifest = receipt_manifest_check()
+    if not manifest["ok"]:
+        raise SystemExit("charged-input SHA-256 mismatch")
+
+    specs = [branch_a_predecessor(), branch_b_ode(), branch_c_consequence()]
+    records = []
+    for spec in specs:
+        runs = [run_system(spec, characteristic) for characteristic in CHARACTERISTICS]
+        records.append({"system": serializable_spec(spec), "runs": runs})
+
+    result = {
+        "manifest_check": manifest,
+        "software": {
+            "python": subprocess.run(
+                ["python3", "--version"], capture_output=True, text=True, check=False
+            ).stdout.strip(),
+            "sympy": sp.__version__,
+            "singular": subprocess.run(
+                ["Singular", "--version"], capture_output=True, text=True, check=False
+            ).stdout.splitlines()[0],
+        },
+        "cores_used_by_driver": 1,
+        "execution": "serial",
+        "per_run_timeout_seconds": 120,
+        "primes": list(PRIMES),
+        "orientation_controls": orientation_controls(),
+        "shape_counts": shape_counts(),
+        "systems": records,
+    }
+    RESULT_PATH.write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + "\n")
+    write_artifact_hashes()
+    print(json.dumps(result, indent=2, sort_keys=True))
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    main()
