@@ -0,0 +1,561 @@
+# Moh `(99,66)`: the radius-two cubic branches after `Omega`
+
+## Verdict first
+
+`MECHANICAL-CHECK`: PASS.  The manifest was generated from the lane receipt
+`xmodel/moh9966-branchB-sol56-20260903.run.v2`; no digest was retyped.  The
+initial `awk`/`sha256sum -c` check returned `OK` for all nine frozen inputs, and
+the independent driver recheck also returned `ok=true`.  The generated manifest
+is `box/moh9966B-20260903/charged-inputs.sha256`.
+
+The useful new result is:
+
+* `DERIVED[PRINTED-LEADER-PREMISE] /
+  SATURATED-EMPTY[FIXED-RADIUS-TWO]`: the omitted radius-two cubic branch C,
+  in which the cubic has three simple roots and the `g` packets are `9+9+9`,
+  is impossible once p.209's `x^15y^40+...` is read, as in the prompt, as the
+  radius-two `T_3` leader.  Moh's Propositions 3.2, 3.3, 4.1 and 6.1 then
+  force a degree-40 leading polynomial to vanish at least 14 times at each of
+  three roots.
+  The exact reduced ideal has reduced basis `[1]` over three primes and over
+  `Q`; a five-term rational unit certificate is recorded below.
+* `REPRESENTATIVE[PRINTED-LEADER-ODE-FACE]`: branch B is not killed by that necessary
+  equation.  It has the exact family
+  `H=z^2(z+3a)`, `R=z^25(z+3a)^14(z-2a)`, `a != 0`.  This is a point of the
+  leading-face variety, not a point of Moh's omitted full coefficient variety
+  and not a Keller pair.
+* `SATURATED-EMPTY[CONTROL-ANSATZ]`: the driver independently reconstructs the
+  charged 14-unknown branch-A predecessor and again obtains `[1]`.  Its bridge
+  to Moh's unprinted ten-coefficient branch-A system remains unproved.
+
+Consequently **“no Keller pair with the `(99,66)` skeleton” is not
+`PROVED-HERE`**.  Its exact status here is
+
+```text
+OPEN[B-FULL-11-VARIABLE-LIFT]
+OPEN[A-PRINTED-10-VARIABLE-BRIDGE]
+OPEN[FROZEN-SOURCE-T3-RADIUS2-LEADER: the p.209 ellipsis is not specified]
+OPEN[PRINCIPAL-MINOR-RADIUS: source does not prove that every split occurs at 2]
+```
+
+At a fixed radius-two place, the partitions `[3]`, `[2+1]`, `[1+1+1]` are
+exhaustive; the last is now excluded.  That is not global exhaustiveness of the
+principal-minor analysis.  In particular, the frozen minor-disc audit already
+keeps the actual `delta_2^*` separate from Moh's major radius `delta_2=1/3`.
+
+## 1. Source reading and page images
+
+The source is the frozen PDF
+`/tmp/jc2-lane.WhlLe3/inputs/moh1983_jram340_configurations_of_roots.pdf`.
+Printed page `p` is PDF page `p-139` (one-based).  The requested images are:
+
+| printed pages | PDF pages | named images |
+|---|---:|---|
+| 150--152 | 11--13 | `box/moh9966B-20260903/pages/moh_pp150_152_pdf-11.png`, `-12.png`, `-13.png` |
+| 207--211 | 68--72 | `box/moh9966B-20260903/pages/moh_pp207_211_pdf-68.png` through `-72.png` |
+
+Supporting pages used for the derivation were also rendered: printed 159, 162,
+164, 170--171, 191--195, and 202 appear under the same `pages/` directory as
+`moh_p159_pdf20.png`, `moh_p162_pdf23.png`, `moh_p164_pdf25.png`,
+`moh_pp170_171_pdf-31.png`, `-32.png`, `moh_pp191_195_pdf-52.png` through
+`-56.png`, and `moh_p202_pdf63.png`.
+
+`SOURCE-READ`, pp.150--152.  Moh defines
+
+```text
+d_1=n, d_{j+1}=gcd(n,M_1,...,M_j),
+q_1=M_1, q_j=M_j-M_{j-1},
+lambda_j=sum_{i<=j} q_i d_i, mu_j=lambda_j/d_j.
+```
+
+For `M=(-66,77,97)` this gives
+
+```text
+d=(99,33,11,1), q=(-66,143,20),
+lambda=(-6534,-1815,-1595), mu=(-66,-55,-145).
+```
+
+Lemma 2.1 gives the Keller terminal index `e=n-1=98`.  Proposition 2.2,
+including its specialization statement, gives monic
+`deg_y T_2^psi=55` and `deg_y T_3^psi=145`, because `77,97<98`.
+
+`SOURCE-READ`, pp.194--195 and 202.  Here `d_3=11`, `v_3=8`, and
+`u_3=d_3-v_3=3`.  The top homogeneous split is therefore
+
+```text
+g_99 = [Y^3(Y-kappa X)^8]^9,
+f_66 = [Y^3(Y-kappa X)^8]^6,
+```
+
+after a linear normalization of the two directions.  Proposition 6.2 gives
+minor/major counts
+
+```text
+             g       f=T_1^psi       T_2^psi
+minor       27           18              15
+major       72           48              40.
+```
+
+The p.202 row gives `V_2=V_3=8`; Definition 5.1 gives the **major** radii
+`(delta_1,delta_2,delta_3)=(4/9,1/3,-1)`.  These are not the actual combined
+minor radius `delta_2^*`.
+
+`SOURCE-READ`, pp.207--211.  Page 207 says only that the first three exceptional
+rows have `u_3=1` and are descended with Propositions 6.3--6.4.  Thus that
+automatic descent does not cover `(99,66)`, whose `u_3=3`.  Page 209 states
+
+```text
+sigma=a_{-1}t^-1+a_0+a_1t+pi t^2,
+g(sigma)=g_sigma(pi)t^-18+...,
+```
+
+and asserts that `g_sigma` is a power of a linear polynomial or the ninth power
+of a cubic with precisely two roots.  For the latter it prints exactly
+
+```text
+Omega: X -> x^-1,
+       Y -> a_0+a_1*x+a_2*x^2+y*x^3,
+Omega(f)       = x^6 y^18 + ...,
+Omega(g)       = x^9 y^27 + ...,
+Omega(T_2^psi) = x^5 y^15 + ...,
+Omega(T_3^psi) = x^15 y^40 + ...,
+J(Omega(f),Omega(g))=x.
+```
+
+The probe still displays `a_{-1}t^-1`, whereas the printed transform starts at
+`a_0`; Moh's phrase “for suitable variables” is the only explanation of that
+absorption on these pages.  This report uses the transform exactly as printed
+and does not invent an additional coordinate formula.
+
+The first sentence of p.210 says that solutions in `k<<x^-1>>` and
+`k<<y^-1>>`, treated by a modified method, reduce the computation to 11
+variables.  It names neither those variables nor their monomial support nor
+their equations.  The displayed computation on pp.210--211 instead concerns
+the different row `(15,10,11,3)`.  The blanket final sentence is not an
+exhibited `(99,66)` computation.
+
+## 2. Why the four printed corners are forced
+
+Put `t=x` after `X=t^-1`.  In Moh's “suitable variables,” after the implicit
+linear normalization that absorbs the minor top term `a_{-1}t^-1`, evaluation
+on the radius-two probe is the exact identity
+
+```text
+Omega(P)(t,(pi-a_2)/t)
+  = P(t^-1,a_0+a_1*t+pi*t^2).
+```
+
+Thus a new-coordinate monomial `x^e y^k` has probe weight `e-k`.  Proposition
+6.1 (pp.191--193) applies because `ord g(sigma)=-18<0`: the same probe is a
+distribution detector for `g,T_1^psi=f,T_2^psi`.  Their degrees have gcd 11,
+and their local degrees are `27,18,15`, so Definition 3.1 gives, for a monic
+cubic `H`,
+
+```text
+g(sigma)   ~ H(pi)^9 t^-18,
+f(sigma)   ~ H(pi)^6 t^-12,
+T_2(sigma) ~ H(pi)^5 t^-10.
+```
+
+Here `~` retains the relevant nonzero leading scalar; compatible
+leading-coefficient normalizations may make the displayed faces monic.
+
+Numerically, `u_3*2-v_3=3*2-8=-2`; multiplying by
+`n/d_3,(-mu_1)/d_3,(-mu_2)/d_3=(9,6,5)` gives the orders
+`-18,-12,-10`.  Thus the powers and orders come from the tower data rather
+than from the printed corners.
+
+This derives `deg H=3`.  A `[2+1]` factorization of `H` consequently gives
+`18+9` roots of `g` in the two at-level packets.  Since two `g` roots then
+separate at radius 2, only `delta_2^* <= 2` follows; equality or attainment for
+the combined product is not inferred.
+
+At the top direction, a degree-`D` polynomial with `r` minor factors contributes
+the Newton face
+
+```text
+x^(4r-D) y^r (x^4 y-kappa)^(D-r).
+```
+
+For `(D,r)=(66,18),(99,27),(55,15)` the corner exponent `4r-D` is respectively
+`6,9,5`.  Proposition 4.6 supplies the top form of `T_3`: if
+`p=Y^3(Y-kappa X)^8`, it is a nonzero scalar multiple of
+`p^13 Y(Y-kappa X)`, hence the minor/major counts
+are `40,105`, and `4*40-145=15`.  This derives all four printed exponent pairs,
+not merely their numerical pattern.
+
+After nonzero leading-coefficient normalizations, for branch B translate the double root to zero and write
+`H(z)=z^2(z+3a)`, `z=xy`, `a!=0`.  The radius-two faces are
+
+```text
+F_2  = y^12 (xy+3a)^6,
+G_2  = y^18 (xy+3a)^9,
+T2_2 = y^10 (xy+3a)^5.
+```
+
+The derived `T3_2` appears in Section 4.  These faces have lower `x`-exponent
+zero and their upper endpoints are the printed `x^6y^18`, `x^9y^27`, and
+`x^5y^15`.
+
+For comparison, selecting one root in branch C with
+`H=z(z-d_1)(z-d_2)` gives Laurent faces
+
+```text
+x^-6 y^6 (xy-d_1)^6(xy-d_2)^6,
+x^-9 y^9 (xy-d_1)^9(xy-d_2)^9,
+x^-5 y^5 (xy-d_1)^5(xy-d_2)^5.
+```
+
+Their upper endpoints are still the three printed monomials.  Therefore those
+monomials alone do not exclude C, and one must not silently assume that every
+`Omega(P)` is polynomial.
+
+Finally, the coordinate determinant is
+
+```text
+det D(X,Y)/D(x,y) = det D(x^-1,a_0+a_1x+a_2x^2+x^3y)/D(x,y) = -x.
+```
+
+If the original constant is `J(f,g)=c`, then
+`J(Omega f,Omega g)=-c*x`; Moh's displayed `+x` fixes `c=-1` (or uses the
+equivalent sign normalization).  The driver checks this orientation and the
+positive controls `J(x^2/2,y)=x`, `J(x^5/5,y)=x^4`.
+
+## 3. Shape from old-coordinate polynomiality
+
+Let `P(X,Y)=sum_{i+j<=D} p_ij X^iY^j`.  Its literal transform is
+
+```text
+Omega(P)=sum p_ij x^-i(a_0+a_1x+a_2x^2+x^3y)^j.                 (3.1)
+```
+
+Conversely, on a monomial,
+
+```text
+Omega^-1(x^e y^k)
+ = X^(k-e) [X^2(Y-a_0)-a_1X-a_2]^k.                            (3.2)
+```
+
+Equations (3.1)--(3.2), not a guessed polygon, are the exact polynomiality
+test: negative `X` powers and terms of total degree greater than `D` must cancel
+after coefficients with the same image are combined.  A single old monomial
+can only produce
+
+```text
+0<=k<=D,             4k-D <= e <= 2D+k,
+```
+
+but membership in this envelope is not sufficient, because inverse-image
+coefficients are correlated.
+
+Combining the top and radius-two weights gives the following useful maximal
+Laurent envelopes:
+
+```text
+F:  max(k-12,4k-66)  <= e <= 132+k, 0<=k<=66;
+G:  max(k-18,4k-99)  <= e <= 198+k, 0<=k<=99;
+T2: max(k-10,4k-55)  <= e <= 110+k, 0<=k<=55;
+T3: max(k-25,4k-145) <= e <= 290+k, 0<=k<=145.
+```
+
+They contain `6187,13816,4316,29441` lattice sites.  If one adds the separate,
+unproved requirement `Omega(P) in k[x,y]`, intersecting with `e>=0` leaves
+`6109,13645,4261,29116` sites.  The branch-C faces displayed above have minimum
+`x`-exponents `-6,-9,-5`, but those face minima are not lower bounds for the
+full Laurent support: for example, an interior old-coordinate monomial may map
+to a more negative pure `x` power without changing either displayed face.
+These are `COUNTING-BOUND` support-site counts, never independent-variable
+counts.
+
+A more stringent calculation shows exactly why the printed information does
+not yield Moh's 11.  In a straightened two-arc **slice**, define
+
+```text
+K(x,w)=x^11 h(x^-1,w/x)=sum_i x^i P_i(w),  deg P_i<=11-i.
+```
+
+The minor order `ord h=-2` requires `i+3j>=9` at `w=0`; the major order
+`ord h=-1/3` requires `3i+4j>=32` at `w=1`.  Hence
+
+```text
+w^3(w-1)^8,
+x^3 w^2(w-1)^6, x^4 w^2(w-1)^5,
+x^6 w(w-1)^4, x^7 w(w-1)^3, x^8 w(w-1)^2,
+x^9(w-1)^2, x^10(w-1), x^11                              (3.3)
+```
+
+is a basis: dimension 9, or eight free coefficients after monicity.  The
+minor initial cubic is
+`pi^3+c_3 pi^2+c_6 pi+c_9`.  Translating its double root to zero gives
+`c_6=c_9=0`; requiring `Omega(h)` polynomial then gives `c_10=0`.  Five
+coefficients remain, with `c_3!=0` distinguishing B from the triple-root
+degeneration, and
+
+```text
+Omega(h)=x*y^3(x^4y-1)^8
+ +c_3*y^2(x^4y-1)^6+c_4*x*y^2(x^4y-1)^5
+ +c_7*y(x^4y-1)^3+c_8*x*y(x^4y-1)^2+c_11.                  (3.4)
+```
+
+`TYPE[GAUGE-SLICE]`: (3.3)--(3.4) are rigorous after straightening the two
+arcs, but p.209 retains `a_0,a_1,a_2` and does not prove that the straightening
+preserves both filtrations and old-coordinate polynomiality.  Thus (3.4) is
+not promoted as Moh's literal ansatz.
+
+The same slice leaves dimensions `103` and `217` for the separate degree-66
+and degree-99 polynomial shapes after `Omega`-polynomiality.  Even fixing all
+three boundary faces leaves strict-interior perturbation spaces of dimensions
+`68` and `165`.  These 233 directions need not satisfy the approximate-root
+relations or the Jacobian, but they prove that the stated order and inverse
+conditions alone do not produce 11 coefficients.  Before any constraints, the
+ordinary monic total-degree arrays have `2277+5049=7326` free coefficients.
+Moh prints 7348 on p.207; this report does not silently identify his counting
+convention with the present monic gauge.
+
+The differing assumption is now precise: Moh additionally invokes an
+unprinted, modified simultaneous root/approximate-root reduction in both
+Laurent fields.  Reconstructing only from his four corners would invent the
+missing h-adic supports.
+
+## 4. The Jacobian face equation and branch B
+
+`DERIVED-SOURCE`.  Proposition 3.2 gives
+
+```text
+deg_y (T_3^psi)_f = -mu_3+M_3 = 145+97 = 242.
+```
+
+Proposition 3.3 applies at this same radius-two place: `M_2,M_3<=e=98`, the
+probe detects `g,f,T_2`, and `ord g<0`.  Consequently
+
+```text
+(T_3^psi)_f(sigma)=c_f H(pi)^22 t^-44+...,  c_f!=0.
+```
+
+This is the formal `f`-derivative, not `T_3` itself, and it is not moved to a
+child place.  From Moh's `x^15y^40` corner together with its minor count 40
+(so its radius-two order is `15-40=-25`), write
+
+```text
+T_3^psi(sigma)=R(pi)t^-25+...,  deg R=40.
+```
+
+Proposition 4.1 applied to `(T_3^psi,g)` and the equality
+`J(T_3^psi,g)=(T_3^psi)_f J(f,g)` now gives, after absorbing a nonzero scalar,
+
+```text
+                 2 H R' - 25 H' R = k H^14,   k!=0.          (4.1)
+```
+
+At a root of `H` of multiplicity `m`, let `r` be its multiplicity in `R`.
+Unless `2r=25m`, comparison in (4.1) gives `r=13m+1`.  For branch B the simple
+root therefore has `r=14`.  At the double root the nonresonant `r=27` would
+already make `deg R>=41`, so resonance is forced and `r=25`.  Scale `R` monic
+and absorb its leading scalar into `k`.  Hence
+
+```text
+H=z^2(z+3a), R=H^12 q,
+q=z^4+q_3z^3+q_2z^2+q_1z+q_0, a!=0,
+2Hq'-H'q-kH^2=0.                                             (4.2)
+```
+
+The six raw coefficients of (4.2) are
+
+```text
+5-k,
+3(-2ak+6a+q_3),
+-9a^2k+12aq_3+q_2,
+6aq_2-q_1,
+-3q_0,
+-6aq_0.
+```
+
+The last is twice `a` times the preceding generator.  The declared ring is
+`Q[a,k,q3,q2,q1,q0,T]`; saturation by `a*k` is represented exactly by adjoining
+`T*a*k-1` and extracting the extended ideal in that ring.
+
+| field | generators incl. wrapper | reduced-basis size | result |
+|---|---:|---:|---|
+| `F_32003` | 6 | 9 | `NONUNIT` |
+| `F_32009` | 6 | 9 | `NONUNIT` |
+| `F_32027` | 6 | 9 | `NONUNIT` |
+| `Q` | 6 | 9 | `NONUNIT` |
+
+The exact solution family is
+
+```text
+k=5, q_3=4a, q_2=-3a^2, q_1=-18a^3, q_0=0,
+q=z(z-2a)(z+3a)^2, T=(5a)^-1.
+```
+
+At `a=1`, direct symbolic substitution gives zero remainder in (4.1):
+
+```text
+H=z^2(z+3), R=z^25(z+3)^14(z-2).
+```
+
+The corresponding bivariate faces are
+
+```text
+T3_2=y^25(xy+3)^14(xy-2), G_2=y^18(xy+3)^9,
+J(T3_2,G_2)=45*x*y^44*(xy+3)^22.
+```
+
+This directly checks the Jacobian-derived face identity.  It is explicitly
+**not** a check of `J(Omega(f),Omega(g))=x`, because no full `F,G` lift has been
+constructed.  Branch B therefore `SURVIVES[NECESSARY-ODE]` but remains
+`OPEN[B-FULL-11-VARIABLE-LIFT]`, not `SURVIVES[KELLER]`.
+
+## 5. Branch C: exact exclusion and saturation certificate
+
+If `H` has three simple roots, resonance is impossible because `2r=25` has no
+integer solution.  Equation (4.1) forces multiplicity 14 at each root, hence
+`deg R>=42`, contradicting `deg R=40`.  This is already a direct branch-C kill.
+
+For a coefficient-system check, work on the squarefree stratum.  If
+`R=H^jR_j`, then (4.1) becomes
+
+```text
+2H R_j' +(2j-25)H'R_j = k H^(14-j).
+```
+
+For `j=0,...,12`, reduction modulo `H` shows `H|R_j`: the integers
+`2j-25` are nonzero and `H'` is a unit modulo squarefree `H`.  Thus
+`R=H^13L`.  Scale `R`, hence `L`, to be monic and absorb that nonzero scalar
+into `k`; then `L` is monic linear and the remaining necessary equation is
+
+```text
+H'L+2HL'-kH=0.                                                (5.1)
+```
+
+Normalize `H=z(z-a)(z-b)`, `L=z+ell`.  The four coefficients of (5.1) are
+
+```text
+f1=5-k,
+f2=(k-4)(a+b)+3ell,
+f3=(3-k)ab-2(a+b)ell,
+f4=ab ell.
+```
+
+The ring is `Q[a,b,ell,k,T]`; the squarefree/nonzero stratum is selected by
+`f5=T*ab(a-b)k-1`.  Singular returns `[1]` in each of `F_32003`, `F_32009`,
+`F_32027`, and `Q`, in 0.016--0.019 seconds per run.  Each run passed the empty
+wrapper, nonempty wrapper, and unsaturated-nonunit controls.
+
+`CERTIFICATE-SIZE`: one polynomial in the reduced basis.  An independently
+expanded rational certificate has five summands and maximum multiplier total
+degree 7.  Put `s=a+b`, `p=ab`, `d=a-b`; then
+
+```text
+m1=T*d*k*(p/2-ell*s), m2=-T*d*k*ell, m3=-T*d*k/2,
+m4=3*T^2*d^2*k^2*ell, m5=-3*T*d*k*ell^2-1,
+1 = m1*f1+m2*f2+m3*f3+m4*f4+m5*f5.
+```
+
+The unsaturated equations deliberately retain the degeneration
+`a=b=ell=0,k=5`, so the unit result is not an artifact of an already-unit raw
+ideal.  Conceptually, (5.1) evaluated at each simple root says `H'(r)L(r)=0`;
+a monic linear polynomial cannot vanish at three distinct roots.  Therefore
+the fixed-radius-two branch C is
+`SATURATED-EMPTY[FIXED-RADIUS-TWO]`, not merely a counting bound.
+
+## 6. Branch-A control
+
+The self-contained control rebuilds the charged predecessor in
+
+```text
+Q[h_0_8,...,h_0_0,bp,bq,br,bs,c,T]
+```
+
+with 14 unknowns excluding `T`:
+
+```text
+h=y^8(y-x)+sum_{j=0}^8 h_0_j y^j,
+A=(h-h|_{y=0})/y, beta=bp*A+bq*y+br*x+bs,
+alpha=quotient_y(beta^2,h),
+f=h^2+2beta, g=h^3+3beta*h+(3/2)alpha.
+```
+
+H-adic extraction of `J(f,g)-c*x^4` gives the charged 29 equations; raw
+expansion gives 36, an extraction-method difference rather than a different
+ansatz.  In both forms the coefficient `-c` occurs.  After adjoining `T*c-1`,
+
+```text
+1=-(T*c-1)-T*(-c).
+```
+
+Thus the certificate has two summands and maximum multiplier degree 1.  All
+three primes and `Q` return `[1]` in under 0.020 seconds and pass the wrapper
+controls.  This exactly reproduces the charged 14-unknown predecessor result.
+
+`TYPE[CONTROL-ONLY]`: Moh does not print the map from every linear-power
+candidate to this 14-unknown predecessor or to his stated ten coefficients.
+The immediate `-c` also shows that this test is a structural ansatz check, not
+the missing computation.  It is not promoted to a proof that branch A itself
+is empty.
+
+## 7. What the exact full system would require
+
+There is a finite first-principles system, but it is not Moh's missing
+11-variable system.  Start with the 7326 old-coordinate coefficients in the
+two monic total-degree arrays and parameters `a_0,a_1,a_2`.  Form `F,G` by
+(3.1); impose all inverse polynomiality relations from (3.2), both Newton
+faces, the universal approximate-root definitions of `T_2^psi,T_3^psi`, and
+every coefficient of
+
+```text
+J(F,G)+c*x=0, c!=0, T*c-1=0
+```
+
+(with the sign convention above).  One must then prove and apply the
+filtration-preserving h-adic/gauge eliminations that map this system to eleven
+variables.  Pp.209--210 omit precisely those eliminations and the resulting
+support.  Saturating an invented eleven-monomial slice would not answer the
+question.
+
+The reduced ODE systems are exact necessary images of that full Jacobian
+system.  Therefore their logical force is asymmetric: emptiness of C lifts to
+the full fixed-radius-two C coefficient branch because every such C candidate
+maps into (5.1), while nonemptiness
+of B does not lift backward without solving all omitted coefficient equations.
+
+There is a second exhaustiveness gap.  P.209 asserts the radius-two description
+but does not prove that principal minor roots cannot first split at another
+admissible radius.  As external corroboration, Yansong Xu, *Intersection
+Numbers and Split of Minor Roots*, [arXiv:1604.07683v4](https://arxiv.org/abs/1604.07683), Section 8, proves the
+three-root exclusion at radius 2 but records a possible `delta=5/2` split and
+describes `(99,66)` as open.  This is `EXTERNAL-CORROBORATION`, not part of the
+frozen-source proof.
+
+## 8. Reproduction and FALLACY-v2 audit
+
+Run serially (one core, 120-second timeout per Singular call):
+
+```text
+python3 box/moh9966B-20260903/moh9966B_driver.py
+```
+
+Primary artifacts are
+
+```text
+box/moh9966B-20260903/moh9966B_driver.py
+box/moh9966B-20260903/moh9966B_results.json
+box/moh9966B-20260903/systems/*.sing
+box/moh9966B-20260903/logs/*.log
+box/moh9966B-20260903/artifacts.sha256
+```
+
+Measured software was Python 3, SymPy 1.12, and Singular 4.3.2.  The driver
+declares every ring and generator order, records the map into each Singular
+ring, and uses the Rabinowitsch extended ideal rather than an unchecked
+`sat()` return wrapper.  Both positive and negative controls are run.  Prime
+marks are nowhere interpreted as derivatives; derivatives are written
+explicitly.
+
+FALLACY-v2: the major radii, radius-two place, and actual combined minor radius
+remain distinct; at-level packet counts do not assert deeper attainment.  The
+branch-B point is typed `REPRESENTATIVE[NECESSARY-ODE-FACE]`, never
+`FULL_ACTUAL_EXIT` or a Keller witness.  No new exit-price assertion is made,
+so no `charge_basis` line is licensed.
